const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout title="Publishing Guide: Reaching Your Audience" activeNav="quest-logs">
  <WikiLayout title="Publishing Guide: Reaching Your Audience" activeNav="quest-logs" activeSidebar="publishing-guide">
    <div class="callout callout-info">
      <strong>📦 Step 4 of 4:</strong> Once your game is finished and tested, the final step is getting it into the hands of real players worldwide.
    </div>

    <h2>Top 7 Publishing Platforms</h2>
    <p>
      Choosing where to release your game depends on your target audience, platform requirements, and budget:
    </p>

    <div class="table-wrapper">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Platform</th>
            <th>Target Audience</th>
            <th>Main Advantages</th>
            <th>Requirements</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Steam</strong></td>
            <td>PC, Mac, Steam Deck</td>
            <td>Largest global PC market, robust discovery algorithms &amp; sales tools<sup>[1]</sup></td>
            <td>$100 submission fee per game, store page setup</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>itch.io</strong></td>
            <td>PC, Web, Indie Fans</td>
            <td>Free to post, open revenue split, perfect for prototypes &amp; jams</td>
            <td>Open registration, zero submission fee</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Epic Games Store</strong></td>
            <td>PC Market</td>
            <td>Dev-friendly revenue split (88/12), front-page curation opportunities</td>
            <td>Submission approval process &amp; Epic SDK integration</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Google Play Store</strong></td>
            <td>Android Devices</td>
            <td>Massive global mobile audience, straightforward publishing access</td>
            <td>One-time $25 developer fee, Android compatibility checks</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Apple App Store</strong></td>
            <td>iOS Devices</td>
            <td>High user monetization across iPhones and iPads</td>
            <td>$99 annual developer fee, strict iOS human interface review</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>Nintendo eShop</strong></td>
            <td>Nintendo Switch</td>
            <td>High consumer demand for portable indie gems</td>
            <td>Official developer application and dev kit approval</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><strong>GOG</strong></td>
            <td>DRM-Free PC Fans</td>
            <td>Dedicated audience valuing DRM-free preservation &amp; classic feel</td>
            <td>Curated editorial selection process</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Pre-Launch Checklist</h2>
    <p>Preparing for a launch starts months before your actual release date:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Launch Your Store Page Early:</strong> Create your public Steam page 6 to 12 months before launch so interested players can start adding your game to their Wishlist<sup>[2]</sup>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cut an Exciting Gameplay Trailer:</strong> Make a short 60-second trailer that shows real gameplay within the first 5 seconds. Avoid long, slow studio logos.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Build a Digital Press Kit:</strong> Assemble high-resolution screenshots, key art posters, animated GIFs, loglines, and developer team details into a public folder. (See our <a href={`${base}blueprints/press-kit/`}>Press Kit Blueprint</a>)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Create a Free Demo:</strong> Build a 15-minute demo build to participate in digital events like Steam Next Fest, driving massive Wishlist growth<sup>[2]</sup>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Translate Your Game Page:</strong> Localize your store description and game menus into popular languages like Simplified Chinese, German, Spanish, and Japanese to reach international players.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Marketing on a Budget</h2>
    <p>
      You do not need a huge marketing budget to get people excited about your game. Focus on creative, visual, community-driven outreach:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Post Short Videos:</strong> Share short, energetic videos on TikTok, YouTube Shorts, and Instagram Reels showing unique mechanics, funny bugs, or satisfying visual moments from development.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reach Out to Niche Streamers:</strong> Email free game keys directly to small and mid-sized Twitch and YouTube creators who regularly stream games in your specific genre.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Leverage Steam Next Fest:</strong> Enter your playable demo into Steam Next Fest. This official event highlights upcoming games on Steam's front page, driving high wishlist conversion rates<sup>[2]</sup>.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Build a Community Discord:</strong> Run a welcoming Discord channel where fans can download test builds, report bugs, share fan art, and chat with you directly.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Launch Day Execution</h2>
    <p>Launch day requires focus, clear communication, and fast responses:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>
        <strong>Publish Your Live Build:</strong> Push the release button on your store dashboard and post launch announcements across social channels, Discord, and email lists.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Track Player Feedback:</strong> Monitor community discussion boards, user review posts, and bug reports closely during the first 24 hours.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deploy Quick Hotfix Patches:</strong> Work quickly to fix critical crashes or game-breaking bugs that players discover in early levels to protect your store review rating.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Send Release Emails:</strong> Contact journalists and content creators who showed interest in your demo to let them know your full game is live.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Engage with Early Players:</strong> Respond politely to user reviews, answer player questions, thank supporters, and share your post-launch update plans.
      </li>
    </ol>

    <div class="callout callout-tip">
      <strong>🎉 Journey Complete:</strong> You now have the full roadmap from concept to launch. Explore our <a href={`${base}equipment/`}>Equipment Tools</a> and <a href={`${base}blueprints/`}>Blueprints</a> to supercharge your project assets!
    </div>

